Stream fixes: heartbeat on connect, multi-client broadcast, pickup-arrived event

- Heartbeat GatewayCommand sent immediately on connect so the stream idles
  correctly instead of flapping every ~10s when there's no trip to dispatch
  yet (the client cancels if nothing at all arrives within its 8s startup
  watchdog).
- VehicleStreamHandler tracked a single 'active_' connection -- whichever
  client (autoware_agent or flutter-ivi, which both connect to this same
  VehicleCommandStream independently) connected most recently silently
  starved the other of every GatewayCommand. Track the full set of
  connected clients and broadcast to all of them instead.
- Forward autoware_agent's TripInitAck (sent exactly when its own trip
  state machine reaches DRIVING_TO_PICKUP -> WAITING_FOR_MOVE, i.e.
  actually arrived at pickup) as a new PickupArrived GatewayCommand so
  flutter-ivi can show the Start Trip button at the right moment.

Upstream-Status: Pending [not yet merged on github.com/Yaquod/iv-cloud-gateway]

